# Principal architect review — B4c

Disposition: APPROVED for the bounded B4c source implementation. No actionable source finding. Increment A, B1–B4c and the C1 record-invariant correction are now accepted at their source checkpoints. This is not campaign-readiness approval.

## Scope and reasoning

LocalRoleRequestFactoryV5._render_rejection_count matches the approved authority chain: the actual current repository checkpoint equals the projection checkpoint, every record is reloaded through authenticated load_experiment and compared exactly, and records must precede the requested round with matching discovery plan/scope/mode. The literal reserved-code invalid-record predicate counts one per committed record. Authentication errors propagate. Existing SearchProjectionV5 membership/order and B3b rejection-event/author/intent binding remain mandatory.

The single cumulative integer is omitted at zero and inserted after all episode metrics, before archive/history evidence. The provider contract already permits failure.* and enforces that citation sequence. The author path rebuilds the same evidence and preserves exact hypothesis citations. No provider, history/novelty, rendering, runtime, record or finalizer source changed in B4c.

Three defaulted summary fields preserve existing positional arguments and add strict nonnegative integer and cross-count validation. Completed lifecycles count record rounds with successful cleanup; evaluated feedback counts their intersection with actual evaluated records carrying campaign evidence; reserved-code invalid records count independently of cleanup. All existing calculations and status meanings remain unchanged.

