## Updated summary-verification result

The implementer's report that both full summary calls failed was accurate for its execution context. Fresh principal calls produced different results:

1. Actual06 returned a full authenticated summary. All three new counts are zero; status=failed, typed_failures=[rendering:stage_failed], role_calls=2, total_tokens=8596, cost_usd=0.04234, cleanup_complete=true. Comparing with its immutable terminal-verification.json matches all 23 historical keys other than command: historical run versus current read-only summarize. The three additional keys are exactly the authorized additions. This is not a same-command before/after pair; principal-actual06-summary-comparison.json records the distinction.
2. Runtime-04 still raised V5CliFailure(artifact_graph_invalid), caused by ValueError(container execution reservation is foreign). Read-only inspection of that real exception frame confirms its command digest matches but executor digest differs:
   - stored: 2849cde885cc8bdde38230bc77ecd17163db42db1b071cc5a8a4212ce4601444
   - current principal process: a72e22fc6deeb4b23f65d82ef32abb148fea4ea6db5efecf26c4391e31605bb9

No check was bypassed and no environment or historical file was changed. Source inspection proves executor identity includes manifest, sandbox profile, owner, mount identity, Docker executable identity, control-directory identity, six allowlisted control-environment entries, runtime contract and repository-root identity. The precise mismatching component has not been isolated. Do not call this proven PATH drift or archive corruption.

The unresolved runtime-04 full-summary comparison is transferred explicitly to Increment C. Acceptance of this additive B4c source change does not waive that readiness dependency or claim complete Task 5 execution evidence.

## Limits and next scope

No real committed render-rejected or exact-duplicate record is available in the bounded four-record inventory. Positive rejection metrics, duplicate/rejection-only/mixed lifecycles, finalized-round paths and positive C1 behavior remain static-reviewed and unexecuted.

This review ran read-only historical authentication/summary projections, source checks and documentation writes only. No tests, synthetic inputs/artifacts, credentials, environment change, paid/model/external calls, candidate evaluation, campaign operation, production edit, commit, push or deployment.

Next session: restore docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-08-pit-optimizer-v5-transition.md and begin its Increment C-a read-only historical-verifier diagnosis. Keep campaign readiness held until the remaining verification issue is resolved or receives a concrete architect decision. No new paid-call budget exists.
